-- Adds an original "About this film" description to every film page.
-- Safe to run again: it only adds the column if missing and overwrites the text.
alter table public.films add column if not exists about text;

update public.films set about = $a$Rebecca is one of the best war photographers in the world, and the work is slowly destroying her family. After she is badly hurt in Afghanistan, she comes home to Ireland, to a husband and two daughters who are done waiting for the call that she won't be coming back. Juliette Binoche gives a searching performance as a woman torn between the people she loves and the stories she believes the world needs to see, with Nikolaj Coster-Waldau as the husband who has run out of patience. Director Erik Poppe drew on his own years as a war photographer. Watch it if you like quiet, serious dramas about the cost of doing what you believe in.$a$ where slug = '1000-times-good-night';
update public.films set about = $a$The college baseball team has one of the longest losing streaks in history, and the university president has finally had enough: the program is getting cut. With their season on the line, a squad of misfits tries everything it can think of to save it, few of those ideas sensible and most of them ridiculous. Bruce Davison and Kate Vernon lead a cast that also includes comedian Josh Blue and baseball great Roger Clemens. It's a loose, rowdy sports comedy in the spirit of Major League, best watched with friends and low expectations about dignity.$a$ where slug = '108-stitches';
update public.films set about = $a$A corporate whistleblower with the FBI on his trail runs as far as he can, to Thailand, hoping to disappear. Bangkok has other plans. Before long he is tangled up with the city's underworld, where the people offering help are rarely the ones he can trust. Colin Egglesfield leads, with Catalina Sandino Moreno, Byron Mann and Stuart Townsend around him. It's a lean fugitive thriller with a strong sense of place: neon streets, humid back rooms and a man who keeps finding out that running is the easy part. A good pick for a night of straightforward suspense.$a$ where slug = 'a-stranger-in-paradise';
update public.films set about = $a$Two best friends are trying to make it as actors in New York, splitting rent, auditions and disappointments. Then they fall for the same woman, and everything they have built together starts to crack. Tyler Hoechlin and Beau Mirchoff play the friends, with Kelen Coleman as the woman between them, under director Malcolm Goodwin. Part comedy and part drama, it's an honest look at ambition, loyalty and the uncomfortable moment when you realise your best friend is also your competition. Worth a watch for anyone who has chased a dream in a big city.$a$ where slug = 'a-true-story';
update public.films set about = $a$Kate is a talented young fashion designer with a mission: save the label her late mother built. To do it, she goes undercover at the rival company run by her stepmother. Portia Doubleday stars, with Chris Noth as her father and Lauren Holly as the stepmother. It's a modern Cinderella story with the glass slipper swapped for a sketchbook: bright, warm and full of fashion-world scheming, with a romance along the way. An easy, feel-good pick for a night in.$a$ where slug = 'after-the-ball';
update public.films set about = $a$Tom Fiorini runs a successful construction company and has a good life, until his foreman goes missing. Tom's decision to fire the wrong man sets off a chain of events that brings violence and hired killers to his door. Anthony Michael Hall leads a tough cast that includes Chris Penn, Tony Danza and Frank Whaley. It's a gritty crime thriller about how fast an ordinary life can come apart when one bad call meets the wrong people. Watch it if you like crime stories where the trouble comes from small choices.$a$ where slug = 'aftermath';
update public.films set about = $a$Gangster Jacques "the Ace" Blinbaum tells the story of his very first con: faking his own kidnapping to squeeze a ransom out of his father. As he talks, this experimental New York fairytale drifts further into fantasy, and it becomes clear the gangster may not be quite what he seems. Made in 1975 by Howard Goldberg, with Tony Azito and Calvert DeForest, it's a strange, playful piece of independent filmmaking from a very different New York. A treat for anyone curious about the offbeat side of 1970s cinema.$a$ where slug = 'apple-pie';
update public.films set about = $a$After a car accident, Sarah starts suffering blackouts and nightmares she can't explain. Unable to trust her own memory, she sets up cameras around the house, and the footage shows her new neighbour letting himself in at night. Katie Walder stars, with Nathan Keyes, Jon Abrahams and Matt Passmore. It's a slow-burn horror thriller that plays on one of the most basic fears there is: that you are not safe in your own home, even while you sleep. Best watched with the lights on.$a$ where slug = 'come-back-to-me';
update public.films set about = $a$Jasmine and Brandon come from rival worlds of dance and would rather not be on the same stage. But a major competition gives them a reason to team up, and they have to learn to trust each other's style before the big night. Kathryn McCormick and Shane Harper lead, with Finola Hughes and David Burtka in support. It's an upbeat musical comedy built on big routines, rivalry and a little romance. A fun pick for dance fans and anyone who grew up on Step Up.$a$ where slug = 'dance-off';
update public.films set about = $a$A group of teenagers heads to a cabin near Donner Pass for a weekend away, the same mountains where the Donner Party was trapped by snow in 1846 and turned to cannibalism. When a storm snows them in, they start disappearing one by one, and the old legend no longer feels like history. Eric Pierpoint stars in this horror film that mixes a classic cabin-in-the-woods setup with one of America's darkest true stories. A good choice for horror fans who like their scares with a local legend attached.$a$ where slug = 'donner-pass';
update public.films set about = $a$John "Falcon" Chapman is a former Marine living with PTSD. When his sister is brutally attacked in the favelas of São Paulo, Brazil, he goes there to find the people responsible, and takes on the criminal network behind them. Martial artist Michael Jai White leads, with Neal McDonough and boxing champion Laila Ali. It's a hard-hitting action film built on real fighting skill, with plenty of hand-to-hand scenes. Watch it if you like old-school action with a lead who can actually do the moves.$a$ where slug = 'falcon-rising';
update public.films set about = $a$Who grows America's food? Director James Moll follows six young farmers and ranchers across the country, people in their twenties who have chosen one of the riskiest jobs there is. The film shows their days, their debts, the weather that can wipe out a year's work, and the reasons they keep going. It's an intimate, respectful documentary that puts real faces on a world most of us only see from the highway. A thoughtful pick for anyone curious about where their food comes from.$a$ where slug = 'farmland';
update public.films set about = $a$Nick DeMaio and his friends have spent their lives playing mob extras in other people's movies. To finally get speaking parts, they stage Shakespeare's Julius Caesar at their local theater on Staten Island. The trouble is, that theater is the hideout of a real gangster the FBI is hunting, and the Feds plant an undercover agent in the cast, mistaking the pretend mobsters for the real thing. Michael Rispoli, Annabella Sciorra, Paul Ben-Victor and Tony Sirico star in a warm, silly comedy of mistaken identity. A treat for fans of mob movies who like to laugh at them too.$a$ where slug = 'friends-and-romans';
update public.films set about = $a$Based on a true story. Catana Starks was a swim coach at Tennessee State University when she became the first woman to coach a college men's golf team. With no scholarships to offer, she recruits an unlikely team of golfers from around the world and guides them toward a record-breaking season. Taraji P. Henson plays Starks, with Tom Felton and Michael Clarke Duncan in support. It's an uplifting sports drama about grit, trust and proving people wrong. A good family pick, especially for anyone who loves an underdog.$a$ where slug = 'from-the-rough';
update public.films set about = $a$Two 14-year-old altar boys have found the perfect scam: serving at funerals gets them out of school, and the rest of the day is theirs for shoplifting, smoking and general trouble. Then a new boy joins them, and the balance of their friendship shifts. Directed by brothers Kevin and Matthew McManus, it's a sharp, funny and surprisingly honest look at being 14, when you're too old to be a kid and too young for anything else. Fans of Stand by Me or Superbad will feel at home.$a$ where slug = 'funeral-kings';
update public.films set about = $a$Walter L. Shaw invented technologies we now take for granted on the telephone, including early forms of conference calling and call forwarding. Yet the Bell system blocked his work, and he never got the credit or the rewards. This documentary, narrated by Frank Langella, tells how his life unravelled, and how his son went down a very different path. It's a gripping true story about invention, big business and what happens when a genius is ignored. Watch it if you like stories behind the things you use every day.$a$ where slug = 'genius-on-hold';
update public.films set about = $a$For two years, director Andrew Marcus followed media provocateur Andrew Breitbart as he took on the mainstream press and the political left, using blogs, video and confrontation to set the news agenda. The documentary shows his tactics up close, from heated public clashes to the stories that made his name. Whatever your politics, it's a revealing look at how online media changed American political news in the early 2010s, and at the man who helped drive that change.$a$ where slug = 'hating-breitbart';
update public.films set about = $a$The survivors of the first haunted hayride massacre thought it was over. It wasn't. Pitchfork, the undead killer, escapes and picks up his spree where he left off, and the survivors have to face him again. This sequel from director Terron R. Parsons, with Sherri Eakin and Jeremy D. Ibanez, keeps the backwoods Halloween setting and the slasher action coming. A good pick for a late-night horror marathon, especially in October.$a$ where slug = 'hayride-2';
update public.films set about = $a$Remy, Augie and Curt have been best friends since birth. When they jokingly make a blood oath and then break it, Curt is dragged down to Hell to be sacrificed. To save him, the other two go after him, through misfit demons, figures from Greek legend and the Devil himself. Nick Swardson, Mila Kunis, Bob Odenkirk, T.J. Miller, Rob Riggle, Susan Sarandon and Danny McBride lend their voices to this stop-motion animated comedy for adults. Irreverent, crude and very funny, it's not for kids.$a$ where slug = 'hell-and-back';
update public.films set about = $a$Marcus is a sleepwalker whose condition makes his nights unpredictable. One morning he wakes up with blood on his hands and no memory of the night before, and a woman he knows has been murdered. Now he has to find out whether he did it. Philip Winchester stars, with Lacey Chabert, Abigail Spencer and Kelly Overton. It's a tense mystery thriller that keeps you guessing alongside its hero, who can't trust the one person he needs to: himself.$a$ where slug = 'in-my-sleep';
update public.films set about = $a$Jake is a filmmaker who decides to make a movie about his own love life. Then the project starts talking back: younger versions of himself at different ages show up, each with advice he doesn't want to hear. Elias Koteas plays Jake, with Jennifer Jason Leigh, Virginia Madsen, Jane Seymour and Mike Vogel. Directed by Howard Goldberg, it's a playful, unusual romantic comedy-drama about the mistakes we keep repeating. A good fit for viewers who like their romances clever and a little strange.$a$ where slug = 'jake-squared';
update public.films set about = $a$A megachurch pastor is worried that his son is drifting away from the faith. His solution: put together a Christian pop group that will reach young people. It does not go to plan. Joel McCrary, Edi Patterson, Mindy Sterling and Octavia Spencer star in this mockumentary-style comedy that pokes good-natured fun at church culture, pop music and the lengths parents will go to. Funny for believers and non-believers alike.$a$ where slug = 'jesus-people';
update public.films set about = $a$Shawn is an automotive designer with a good life, until he receives a cryptic message: a curse has followed his family for generations, and now it has come for him. To protect his family, he has to confront an ancient jinn, a spirit from Middle Eastern lore. Dominic Rains, Serinda Swan, Ray Park, William Atherton and Faran Tahir star. Writer-director Ajmal Zaheer Ahmad blends supernatural horror with action and fantasy. Watch it if you want something different from the usual ghost story.$a$ where slug = 'jinn';
update public.films set about = $a$When the Saran family in New Jersey loses money in a scam, everyone has to pitch in, including their son, who works at a call center in India. As the two halves of the family's world collide, they pull together in ways none of them expected. Samrat Chakrabarti and Darshan Jariwala star in this warm comedy-drama about family, money and the strange ways the global economy connects people. A good pick for anyone who loves stories about immigrant families.$a$ where slug = 'karma-calling';
update public.films set about = $a$Three college slackers are about to fail their professor's class. Their only way to save their grades is to beat him at his favourite hobby, live-action role-playing, where he plays the villain Derek the Unholy. Foam swords, capes and grudges follow. Evan Williams, Jesse Reid and Scott Patey star, with comedian Brian Posehn. It's a goofy, good-hearted comedy about LARPing and the people who love it. Perfect for anyone who has ever had a nerdy hobby.$a$ where slug = 'lloyd-the-conqueror';
update public.films set about = $a$A young Christian woman is attacked by a mechanic and becomes pregnant. Years later, she makes a choice that shakes her family: she reaches out to the man, now in prison. Christine Kelly and Stephen Baldwin star in this faith-based drama about trauma, forgiveness and whether anyone is beyond grace. It handles a hard subject seriously. A good fit for viewers looking for a thought-provoking film about faith in the hardest circumstances.$a$ where slug = 'loving-the-bad-man';
update public.films set about = $a$Travis Woodson is a divorced architect and devoted father of two, and his unruly dog Lucky has a habit of wrecking his dates. When Travis starts falling for fellow architect Amber, Lucky falls for her dog Amy. But the two architects end up competing for the same design job, and the wealthy client has his eye on Amber. It's up to Lucky and Amy to bring their owners together. Bryce Johnson, Boti Bliss, Cat Deeley and Lara Flynn Boyle star in a sweet family comedy. Ideal for dog lovers of every age.$a$ where slug = 'lucky-dog';
update public.films set about = $a$A woman is caring for her husband after a bar fight left him unable to look after himself. As the strain grows, she is drawn back toward his brother, the boy she loved when they were young. Brandon Routh, Erin Cottrell and Jordan Belfi star in this quiet drama about loyalty, guilt and the life you might have had. Watch it if you like intimate love stories that take the hard questions seriously.$a$ where slug = 'missing-william';
update public.films set about = $a$A mad scientist's experiment goes wrong, and the family dog Max turns into a giant monster mutt. Now the children have to protect him from the people hunting him, and find a way to change him back. Rhiannon Leigh Wryn, Billy Unger and Bart Johnson star in this family comedy-adventure. It's light, silly and full of heart, a good pick for a family movie night with younger kids.$a$ where slug = 'monster-mutt';
update public.films set about = $a$Dave Navarro, guitarist for Jane's Addiction, was 15 when his mother was murdered by her former boyfriend. Her killer avoided capture for eight years, while Navarro faced his fears through drugs, art and escape. In this documentary he goes back to the events that changed his life, speaking with friends, family, police and FBI agents to come to terms with her murder and with the reality of domestic violence. A powerful, personal film. Viewer discretion advised.$a$ where slug = 'mourning-son';
update public.films set about = $a$Norman is a high school student whose mother has died and whose father is dying. When a rumour spreads that Norman himself has cancer, he doesn't correct it, and a new relationship begins to grow on the lie. Dan Byrd, Emily VanCamp, Richard Jenkins and Adam Goldberg star. It's a funny, painful and very human drama about grief and the strange ways people cope. Watch it if you like coming-of-age films with real emotional weight.$a$ where slug = 'norman';
update public.films set about = $a$Lancashire, 1974. Two teenagers escape a grey small-town life through the music they find in all-night clubs: rare American soul records, played to crowds who dance until dawn. Elliot James Langridge and Joshua Whitehouse star, with Antonia Thomas and Steve Coogan. Director Elaine Constantine brings the Northern Soul scene to life with real energy: the records, the clothes, the moves and the obsession. A must for music lovers, and anyone who remembers what it felt like when a song changed everything.$a$ where slug = 'northern-soul';
update public.films set about = $a$On a flight home to Chicago for a family wedding, childhood friends Josh and Molly agree to fake an engagement, so that Josh's dying father can meet the woman his son will marry. As both families start planning the phony wedding, the act starts to feel real. Shane McRae and Aubrey Dollar star, with Daniel J. Travanti and Robert Belushi. It's a charming, funny romantic comedy with plenty of family chaos. Perfect for fans of the fake-relationship trope.$a$ where slug = 'one-small-hitch';
update public.films set about = $a$In an alternate 1985, America is ruled by an authoritarian president. Nick Brady, a record store clerk, begins receiving visions from a mysterious entity called VALIS, and is drawn into a plot to expose the regime. Based on the novel by Philip K. Dick, the film stars Jonathan Scarfe, Shea Whigham, Alanis Morissette and Katheryn Winnick. It's thoughtful science fiction about paranoia, faith and resistance. A must for Philip K. Dick fans.$a$ where slug = 'radio-free-albemuth';
update public.films set about = $a$Two men who have nothing in common set out across Texas together: one is on the run from a loan shark's enforcers, the other has just been released. Over the miles, both have to face what they're running from. Morgan Simpson and Michael Clarke Duncan star, with Taryn Manning and Luke Perry, under director Mario Van Peebles. It's a soulful road movie about second chances, with plenty of blues along the way.$a$ where slug = 'redemption-road';
update public.films set about = $a$Filmed over five years in 25 countries on 70mm film, Samsara is a journey without words. Director Ron Fricke takes you through sacred places, disaster zones, factories and natural wonders, connected by the theme of the cycle of birth, death and rebirth. There is no narration and no story, just extraordinary images and music. It's one of the most beautiful documentaries ever made, best watched on the biggest screen you have with the sound up.$a$ where slug = 'samsara';
update public.films set about = $a$Eric Schultz is the most popular student at Lake O'Dell High School. Then his guidance counsellor, Sylvia Martin, makes him an offer he can't refuse: to graduate, he has to complete a list of her own high school fantasies. As he works through her regrets, his place on the school's A-list starts to slip. Hudson Thames and Alyson Stoner star, with Hal Sparks. It's a light teen comedy about popularity and figuring out who you are when it's gone.$a$ where slug = 'the-a-list';
update public.films set about = $a$Jaden Miller is a struggling auto mechanic in the Bronx, and he and his mother are close to losing their home. Boxing looks like the only way out. When he meets legendary trainer Duane Taylor, Jaden sees his chance to fight his way out of poverty and go for a title. Kent Moran writes, directs and stars, with Michael Clarke Duncan, in one of his final roles, as Taylor, and S. Epatha Merkerson and Justin Hartley. A heartfelt boxing drama for anyone who loves Rocky.$a$ where slug = 'the-challenger';
update public.films set about = $a$In 1830, the violinist Niccolò Paganini is the most famous musician in Europe, steered by his scheming manager Urbani. Lured to London for his British debut, he falls for the daughter of his host. Real-life violin virtuoso David Garrett plays Paganini, performing the music himself, with Jared Harris, Joely Richardson and Christian McKay. Directed by Bernard Rose, it's a lavish period drama about genius, fame and temptation. Music lovers shouldn't miss the concert scenes.$a$ where slug = 'the-devils-violinist';
update public.films set about = $a$Alice Harvey is a 28-year-old assistant book editor in New York. When she is assigned to the reissue of a celebrated novel, she has to face its author, Milan Daneker, the older writer who befriended her as a teenager and turned their relationship into his book. The memories she has buried start to unravel her present. Emily VanCamp and Michael Nyqvist star. Written and directed by Marya Cohn, it's a sensitive, serious drama about power, memory and reclaiming your own story.$a$ where slug = 'the-girl-in-the-book';
update public.films set about = $a$Jack Maldonado is ambitious and full of misguided nostalgia. He buys a small apartment building in the Bronx and moves his big, loud family in rent-free. Tension builds as he pushes his ideas on everyone, all while hiding that his corner store is a front for selling marijuana. E. J. Bonilla and Melissa Fumero star in this 2013 family drama from director Henry Barrial. It's a lively, heartfelt picture of family, loyalty and a man who wants to be the hero of everyone's story.$a$ where slug = 'the-house-that-jack-built';
update public.films set about = $a$Teenagers Billy and Allie find a lost medallion that sends them back 200 years to an island kingdom ruled by a tyrant. To get home, they have to help the islanders defeat him and find the medallion's missing half. Billy Unger and Sammi Hanratty star, with James Hong and Alex Kendrick. It's a family adventure with treasure, sword fights and a message about courage and faith. A good pick for families with kids aged 8 and up.$a$ where slug = 'the-lost-medallion';
update public.films set about = $a$A laid-off dock worker goes to the luxurious mansion of the industrialist who put him and 200 of his colleagues out of work, and takes a bloody revenge. Then he settles into his victim's life. But paranoia sets in, and a mysterious figure in an orange jacket begins to stalk him. From Latvian director Aik Karapetian, this is a stylish, unsettling horror thriller about class, guilt and the ghosts we bring on ourselves. Not for the faint-hearted.$a$ where slug = 'the-man-in-the-orange-jacket';
update public.films set about = $a$Suburbia, 1975. Four children retreat to the attic and tell each other stories, while downstairs their parents' dinner party slowly falls apart over the course of one night. John Hawkes and Molly Parker star in this quiet, observant drama from director Julia Dyer. It captures how children see far more of the adult world than adults think, and how they build their own worlds to cope with it. A rewarding watch for fans of thoughtful family dramas.$a$ where slug = 'the-playroom';
update public.films set about = $a$When Emily Parris exposes a secret society of teenage girls who meet in the woods at night, she sends their small town into hysteria, a modern-day Salem witch trial played out through social media and rumour. The mystery deepens because every accused girl has taken a vow of silence. Georgie Henley, Kara Hayward and Kal Penn star. It's a gripping mystery about friendship, secrets and how quickly a community turns on its own. Great for fans of teen thrillers with substance.$a$ where slug = 'the-sisterhood-of-night';
update public.films set about = $a$Steven Ray is a violent hit man grieving a personal tragedy. Percival is a grief-stricken man who has tried and failed to end his own life many times. Percival hires Steven to kill him, but survives every attempt, and Steven begins to believe Percival may be cursed and unable to die. Steve Mouzakis and Leon Cain star in this dark, unusual Australian thriller about loss and fate. Contains themes of suicide; viewer discretion advised.$a$ where slug = 'the-suicide-theory';
update public.films set about = $a$Carl takes his wife Sue on a romantic ski weekend to win her back. Then he discovers the lodge is run by his ex-girlfriend Robyn, and before long Sue's own ex shows up too. Sam Huntington, Meaghan Rath and Emmanuelle Chriqui star in this Canadian romantic comedy about marriage, old flames and awkward breakfasts. It's funny, frank and a bit messy, like real relationships. A good pick for a couples' movie night.$a$ where slug = 'three-night-stand';
update public.films set about = $a$After her father is murdered, teenager Davey Wexler moves with her mother and brother to Los Alamos, New Mexico. Lost in grief, she finds her way slowly, helped by a young man called Wolf. Based on the novel by Judy Blume, adapted with her son Lawrence Blume, who directs. Willa Holland stars, with Amy Jo Johnson and Tatanka Means. It's a tender coming-of-age drama about loss and healing, set against the desert landscape. A must for Judy Blume fans.$a$ where slug = 'tiger-eyes';
update public.films set about = $a$Allied prisoners of war in a Japanese camp in Burma are forced to build a railway. To keep their spirits alive, some of them start a secret school, and a fierce debate grows among the prisoners: does survival mean submission or resistance? Based on Ernest Gordon's true memoir, the film stars Ciarán McMenamin, Robert Carlyle, Kiefer Sutherland and Mark Strong. This is the Director's Cut. A powerful war drama about faith, cruelty and forgiveness.$a$ where slug = 'to-end-all-wars';
update public.films set about = $a$Ellie and her friends come back from a camping trip in the Australian bush to find their country invaded and their families taken prisoner. With no adults left to help, the teenagers start fighting back as guerrillas. Based on John Marsden's much-loved novel, the film stars Caitlin Stasey, Rachel Hurd-Wood and Phoebe Tonkin, under director Stuart Beattie. It's a thrilling action-adventure about courage and friendship. A great pick for teens and fans of The Hunger Games.$a$ where slug = 'tomorrow-when-the-war-began';
update public.films set about = $a$In a dusty attic, toys left behind by children have their own world. But when the cat and the forces of the Land of Evil threaten Buttercup, one of their own, her friends set out to rescue her. From Czech animator Jiří Barta, with English voices by Forest Whitaker, Joan Cusack and Cary Elwes, it's a handmade stop-motion fairy tale full of charm and invention. A lovely discovery for families and animation fans.$a$ where slug = 'toys-in-the-attic';
update public.films set about = $a$An archaeologist teams up with a guard of the Vatican's secret treasure order to race ruthless treasure hunters to a legendary relic: the Seal of Solomon. Anna Friel, Raoul Bova and Sean Brosnan star in this globe-trotting adventure full of riddles, chases and ancient legends. Fans of Indiana Jones and National Treasure will find plenty to enjoy.$a$ where slug = 'treasure-guards';
update public.films set about = $a$In a small Ohio town hit by hard times, the high school football team can't seem to win. A new coach arrives to turn the program around, and the town hopes he can turn it around too. D.B. Sweeney, William Mapother, Natalie Imbruglia and Maddie Hasson star. It's a heartfelt small-town sports drama about second chances, community and Friday night lights. A good family pick for football fans.$a$ where slug = 'underdogs';
update public.films set about = $a$Bryson is a pet photographer who is forced to marry the daughter of a Croatian gangster to settle a debt. Then, on their honeymoon in Tahiti, the bride is kidnapped. Dave Annable and Katharine McPhee star, with Rob Schneider, Mena Suvari and Kathy Bates. It's an action-packed romantic comedy with exotic settings, mob trouble and plenty of laughs. A good pick for a light, fun night.$a$ where slug = 'you-may-not-kiss-the-bride';
update public.films set about = $a$A group of college friends head to a lakeside cabin for a weekend of fun. But a chemical spill has contaminated the water, and the local beavers have turned into zombie predators. Rachel Melvin, Cortney Palm and Lexi Atkins star, with Rex Linn. It's exactly what the title promises: a gleefully gory, self-aware horror comedy with plenty of bad puns. A cult favourite for midnight movie fans.$a$ where slug = 'zombeavers';
